# Paths whose change requires a devil's-advocate pass before `ship.sh land` (R78).
# One extended-regex per line, matched against changed paths. No file ⇒ no gate.
#
# Scope: everything that BEARS BEHAVIOUR. Widened 2026-07-29 after an audit found the gate had
# real holes — `hooks.json` (registering a hook), `tests/` (weakening a test IS "a green gate
# certifying broken work", R78's own premise) and `.github/` (CI could be disabled outright) all
# shipped ungated. Pure prose (docs/*.md, README) stays OUT on purpose: a gate that fires on a
# typo trains a reflexive "clean", and a rubber stamp launders the decision instead of testing it.
^plugins/[^/]+/(bin|lib)/
^check\.sh$
^plugins/[^/]+/(hooks|commands)/
# the verification kit: it no longer ships, but weakening a gate or a test is exactly what R78
# exists to challenge — the move out of the plugin must not move it out of scrutiny.
^dev/
^plugins/[^/]+/STEERING\.md$
^\.github/
# the manifests decide what actually gets INSTALLED
^\.claude-plugin/
^plugins/[^/]+/\.claude-plugin/
# the gate's own config: weakening this must itself be challenged
^\.companion/da-paths$
